==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dark Rider Valkyrie '''at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Li'l Valkyrie Dark's purpose is similar to that of [[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie]] and [[D'artanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|Meow-sketeer]]: she is a quick midrange rusher with high DPS. Compared to her light form, she has half the damage and significantly fewer abilities, but in return has a 100% chance to perform a level 3 [[Wave Attack]]. Losing the abilities may seem like she is inferior to the original, but it is important to understand the value of each of them. While most of Li'l Valkyrie's are nice, it is only really Zombie Killer and Barrier Breaker that greatly improve her general usage; additionally, Curse immunity literally does nothing while Knockback and Warp immunity occasionally harm her already poor survivability due to denying her opportunities to reposition.

In comparison to Li'l Valkyrie's abilities, Li'l Valkyrie Dark's Wave Attack is by far the most important one. This gives her piercing range even higher than Meow-sketeer's, but without the blindspot! Her halved attack is also offset by the wave: she still does 11k DPS to frontline enemies unless her first hit knocks them back, while being able to deal 5.5k DPS to the enemy backlines.

Unfortunately, she is not without her weaknesses. She still suffers from poor survivability due to having only 2 knockbacks, low HP and low range. Her high speed combined with somewhat long foreswing and her time between attacks not being entirely backswing can cause her to rush into enemies who can shred her in seconds. Even with that, she often outperforms the original Li'l Valkyrie, but keep in mind that Meow-sketeer and [[D'arktanyan (Uber Rare Cat)|D'arktanyan]] typically outclass her by a wide margin.

