==Trivia==
*Li'l Valkyrie Dark is one of the only Cats whose appearance differs between versions, like her [[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|normal counterpart]].
*[[Valkyrie Cat (Special Cat)|True Valkyrie Cat]]'s [[Media:024 c HD.png|unused wing design]] was later used for Li'l Valkyrie's and Li'l Valkyrie Dark's wing designs, albeit smaller and with less detail. Li'l Valkyrie Dark's wings use said unused design, but with a darker color.
*On the initial release of Version 9.0 for every version of The Battle Cats except for the Japanese one, Dark Rider Valkyrie's appearance both in the Cat Guide and in Battle was glitched due to PONOS using the animation data for her Japanese version.
*Prior to [[Version 14.5 Update|Version 14.5]], Li'l Valkyrie Dark's English descriptions had an error, as they claimed she blocked Waves instead of being immune to them.
*Li'l Valkyrie Dark is labeled as a Special Cat in The Battle Cats Unite.
*She, [[Nekondo (Special Cat)|Nekondo]], [[Baozi Cat (Special Cat)|Baozi Cat]], [[Crazed Baozi Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Baozi Cat]], and [[Li'l Valkyrie (Uber Rare Cat)|Li'l Valkyrie]] are part of a version exclusive In The Battle Cats Unite, that being the Southeast Asia version of the game.
**She can be obtained in the Japanese version, however, only through save file editing and thus cannot be playable through natural means.

